In `ExtensionEngine.get_loc`, after the `over_size_threshold` branch, the code has:
```
if not self.unique:
    return self._get_loc_duplicates(val)
return self._get_loc_duplicates(val)
```
Both branches call `_get_loc_duplicates`, so the uniqueness check is useless. When the index is unique and not over the size threshold, it should do a direct lookup (e.g. via `_maybe_get_bool_indexer`) rather than always going through the duplicate path. This mirrors the same bug in `NullableEngine.get_loc`.
